DwarfSpec Save-Game Mount Implementation
=========================================

Purpose:
    ☐ Add `ds.mountSaveGame(directory_name)` for selecting the save used by live DwarfSpec automation.
    ☐ Ensure that the requested save is loaded when the command returns successfully.
    ☐ Leave the requested save loaded after the example finishes.

Completion contract:
    ☐ Complete every applicable implementation, test, declaration, documentation, package, and live-evidence item below.
    ☐ Treat this checklist as the source of truth for implementation status.
    ☐ Preserve unrelated worktree and index changes; do not stash or commit user changes.
    ☐ Keep focused unit, full unit, Lua syntax, package, and live DFHack evidence distinct in the final handoff.

Command contract:
    ☐ Export `ds.mountSaveGame(directory_name)`.
    ☐ Accept exactly one nonempty save-directory name.
    ☐ Read the currently loaded save directory when a world is loaded.
    ☐ Do nothing when the requested save is already loaded.
    ☐ When a different world is loaded, unload it without saving.
    ☐ Load the requested save after the current world has unloaded.
    ☐ When no world is loaded, load the requested save directly.
    ☐ Return only after the requested save is confirmed as loaded.
    ☐ Leave the requested save loaded; do not register example cleanup that unloads it, restores the previous save, or returns to the title screen.
    ☐ Report validation, unload, load, wrong-save, and timeout failures with useful bounded diagnostics.

Non-goals:
    ☐ Do not add save-or-discard policy options.
    ☐ Do not save the current world before unloading it.
    ☐ Do not restore the previously loaded world after the command or example.
    ☐ Do not return to the title screen as example cleanup.
    ☐ Do not treat the loaded save as an owned DwarfSpec resource.
    ☐ Do not add save fixture generation, copying, renaming, deletion, migration, or reset behavior.
    ☐ Do not load inactive worlds that the underlying Dwarf Fortress load path cannot select.

Phase 0 - Confirm the runtime boundary:
    ☒ Record the active checkout, branch, worktree state, installed rock version, and package contents before editing.
        - Evidence: `world-mount-system` at `ead0763`; worktree and index were clean. LuaRocks has `dwarfspec 0.2.0-1` installed. `dist/dwarfspec-0.2.0-1.all.rock` contains 92 entries, including `lua/dwarfspec/ds.lua`, and no test entries.
    ☒ Record the existing `ds.getSaveDirectoryName()` implementation, declaration, unit coverage, live coverage, and documentation.
        - Evidence: the implementation is in `src/dwarfspec/ds.lua`; the declaration is in `src/ds.d.lua`; coverage is in `tests/unit/ds_mount_commands_spec.lua` and `tests/automation/ds_export_live_spec.lua`; the command table is in `README.md`.
    ☒ Confirm the DFHack APIs and state-change events used to determine whether a world is loaded and which save directory it uses.
        - Evidence: `dfhack.isWorldLoaded()` is the world-loaded predicate and `dfhack.world.ReadWorldFolder()` returns the loaded directory. DFHack publishes `SC_WORLD_LOADED` and `SC_WORLD_UNLOADED`; direct predicate and directory reads remain the command's authoritative checks.
    ☒ Confirm that raw-frame waits continue across world unload and load.
        - Evidence: DwarfSpec schedules ordinary waits with `dfhack.timeout(..., 'frames', ...)`. DFHack stores frame timers separately and cancels only tick timers on `SC_WORLD_UNLOADED`; raw-frame callbacks therefore remain available during the transition.
    ☒ Confirm the supported screens from which the installed `load-save` command can load a requested save.
        - Evidence: DFHack 53.15-r1 `scripts/load-save.lua` accepts an existing `viewscreen_loadgamest`, or a `viewscreen_titlest` containing the `Continue` choice, then defers its final `SELECT` by one raw frame.
    ☒ Confirm a stable mechanism for choosing `QUIT_WITHOUT_SAVING` without localized text, pixel coordinates, or resolution assumptions.
        - Evidence: `df.main_menu_option_type.QUIT_WITHOUT_SAVING` is a generated enum value. The native options interface exposes its current `option` vector and dedicated fortress/adventure confirmation flags, allowing the adapter to locate the action by enum identity rather than rendered text or coordinates. Phase 2 will validate the corresponding input sequence against a disposable live save.
    ☒ Record the focused and full pre-change test baselines.
        - Evidence: focused current-save unit coverage: 1 success, 0 failures, 0 errors; full unit suite: 530 successes, 0 failures, 0 errors; Lua syntax and formatting: 253 files; safe live export suite: 2 successes, 0 failures, 0 errors, `cleanup_confirmed=true`.

Phase 1 - Implement current-save comparison and validation:
    ☒ Validate that `directory_name` is a string containing one nonempty directory name.
        - Evidence: `save_game_mount.validate_directory_name()` accepts exactly one nonempty string.
    ☒ Reject path separators, absolute paths, current-directory names, parent-directory names, and traversal attempts.
        - Evidence: validation rejects separators, drive-qualified names, `.` and `..`, and embedded NUL bytes without rendering the supplied name.
    ☒ Reject extra arguments.
        - Evidence: validation receives the exact argument count and rejects every count other than one.
    ☒ Read `dfhack.isWorldLoaded()` before deciding whether an unload is needed.
        - Evidence: the injected `is_world_loaded` predicate is required and is evaluated before any directory read.
    ☒ Read the loaded directory through `dfhack.world.ReadWorldFolder()` when a world is loaded.
        - Evidence: the injected `read_world_folder` function is required only for the loaded-world path and its result is validated.
    ☒ Return immediately without unload, load, or cleanup registration when the loaded directory exactly matches the request.
        - Evidence: matching preflight returns `transition_required=false`; its focused test proves no cleanup registration occurs.
    ☒ Add focused tests for valid names, invalid names, extra arguments, unloaded state, matching state, and differing state.
        - Evidence: `tests/unit/save_game_mount_spec.lua` covers all listed cases, including missing DFHack APIs and malformed loaded-directory results.

Phase 2 - Implement discard and unload:
    ☒ Accept native mouse selection for the enum-identified discard action.
        - Evidence: a controlled live probe opened the native options overlay in `TestWorld 01`, found `QUIT_WITHOUT_SAVING` as visible ordinal 4, clicked its computed row at grid coordinate `(132, 42)` in a `264x75` window, and observed `fort_quit_without_saving_confirm=true` while the world remained loaded.
    ☒ Open the required native options state through stable input when a different world is loaded.
    ☒ Select `QUIT_WITHOUT_SAVING` by generated enum identity and click its computed native button row.
    ☒ Approve any required discard confirmation through stable native input.
        - Evidence: the destructive live probe clicked the confirmation action at computed grid coordinate `(106, 41)`. After 1.5 seconds, `dfhack.isWorldLoaded()` was false, the active screen was `viewscreen_titlest`, focus was `title/Default`, and the options interface was closed.
    ☒ Wait across raw frames until `dfhack.isWorldLoaded()` is false.
    ☒ Use bounded timeouts that include the requested directory, observed directory, focus, viewscreen, and elapsed time.
    ☒ Restore temporary input and pointer-tracking state used while initiating the unload.
    ☒ Add focused adapter tests for success, confirmation, timeout, unexpected screen state, temporary-input cleanup, click geometry, and invalid geometry.
        - Evidence: focused `save-game unload adapter` coverage reports 12 successes, 0 failures, and 0 errors. The complete standalone unit suite reports 547 successes, 0 failures, and 0 errors. Lua 5.4.6 syntax and formatting checks pass for 257 files.

Phase 3 - Implement requested-save loading:
    ☐ Reach or verify a screen from which the installed `load-save` command can run.
    ☐ Invoke `load-save` with the validated directory name as one exact argument.
    ☐ Account for the script deferring save selection by one raw frame.
    ☐ Capture immediate errors for missing, inactive, incompatible, or unavailable saves.
    ☐ Wait across raw frames until a world is loaded.
    ☐ Read the resulting directory through `dfhack.world.ReadWorldFolder()`.
    ☐ Require the resulting directory to exactly match the requested directory.
    ☐ Fail with bounded diagnostics when loading times out or a different directory becomes loaded.
    ☐ Leave the successfully loaded requested save in place.
    ☐ Add focused tests for successful loading, deferred selection, script failure, timeout, and wrong-save detection.

Phase 4 - Export and document the command:
    ☐ Wire the implementation into the run-scoped `ds` namespace.
    ☐ Implement `ds.mountSaveGame(directory_name)` with a language-appropriate documentation comment.
    ☐ Add language-appropriate documentation comments for every new production class and method.
    ☐ Keep `ds.getSaveDirectoryName()` unchanged.
    ☐ Add the public declaration to `src/ds.d.lua`.
    ☐ Document the no-op behavior when the requested save is already loaded.
    ☐ Document that a different loaded world is discarded without saving.
    ☐ Document that the requested save remains loaded after the example and becomes the starting state for subsequent examples or runs.
    ☐ Add export and command-delegation coverage.

Phase 5 - Verify unit and live behavior:
    ☐ Prove with focused unit tests that a matching save performs no unload or load.
    ☐ Prove with focused unit tests that a differing save performs unload before load.
    ☐ Prove with focused unit tests that an unloaded game performs only the load path.
    ☐ Prove with focused unit tests that the command confirms the resulting directory before returning.
    ☐ Define two explicitly disposable active automation saves, A and B, outside the public command.
    ☐ Add a safe live test for mounting the already-loaded save.
    ☐ Add a separately selected destructive live test that mounts B while A is loaded.
    ☐ Confirm that A is discarded without saving and B is loaded.
    ☐ Confirm that B remains loaded after the example finishes.
    ☐ Run the command again for B and confirm that it is a no-op.
    ☐ Run and record focused unit tests.
    ☐ Run and record the full standalone unit suite separately.
    ☐ Run and record Lua syntax and formatting checks separately.
    ☐ Run and record selected live tests separately from the complete live suite.
    ☐ Run and record `git diff --check`.

Phase 6 - Verify packaging and final acceptance:
    ☐ Update the LuaRocks package manifest for every new production module and declaration artifact.
    ☐ Build the release rock through the repository publish tooling.
    ☐ Inspect the archive contents directly.
    ☐ Require every new production module and public declaration in the archive.
    ☐ Reject tests, fixture saves, generated logs, and temporary artifacts from the archive.
    ☐ Load the built artifact in the controlled DFHack environment.
    ☐ Re-run the safe same-save test against the packaged artifact.
    ☐ Re-run the selected A-to-B transition against the packaged artifact.
    ☐ Confirm that B remains loaded after final verification.
    ☐ Confirm the DFHack process is responsive, the executor is idle, the queue is empty, quarantine is absent, mounts are clear, pointer tracking is restored, and no buttons remain pressed.
    ☐ Record exact commands, results, fixture identities, package path, archive audit, and final runtime state below.

